 ],
 "literal": "Swelling mountain pools dried up, at the beginning of the impoverished desert path, / the fragrant blossoms on the twigs of the young sirissa tree, / appearing like the crest on the head of a gentle peacock, / in this long forest path, she too, with us, / if she has agreed to unite in marriage, / indeed good, O heart, is your desired resolve!",
 "translation": "At the start of the impoverished desert path where the swelling mountain pools have dried up, the fragrant blossoms on the twigs of the young sirissa tree look like the crest on the head of a gentle peacock. In this long forest path, if she has agreed to unite in marriage and come with us, then, O heart, your desired resolve is indeed very good!",
 "modern": "நீர் நிறைந்த சுனைகள் காய்ந்துபோன வறண்ட பாலை நிலத்தின் தொடக்கத்தில், இளமையான வாகை மரத்தின் கிளைகளில் உள்ள மணமுள்ள மலர்கள், மென்மையான மயிலின் தலையிலுள்ள கொண்டையைப் போலத் தோன்றுகின்றன. இத்தகைய நீண்ட காட்டு வழியில், இவளும் நம்மோடு இணைந்து மணம் செய்துகொள்ள உடன்பட்டாள் என்றால், நெஞ்சமே! அவளை அழைத்துவர விரும்பிய உன்னுடைய துணிவு மிகவும் நல்லதே!",
 "explanation": "The hero is speaking to his own heart during their elopement through the desert path (pālai). He observes the harshness of the dry desert where mountain pools have dried up, yet he notices the beautiful, fragrant blossoms of the young vākai tree that resemble the crest of a gentle peacock. He feels reassured and comforted by the heroine's willingness to accompany him through this difficult terrain. He praises his own heart for having the courage and resolve to bring her along, realizing that her love and presence make the arduous journey beautiful. The contrast between the dry desert and the beautiful peacock-like blossoms reflects the transformation of a harsh landscape through love.",
